# Development loop

Never code first and document later. For every subsystem slice:

```
Idea
  → Engineering Notebook (requirements, architecture, interfaces)
  → Cursor implements exactly that subsystem
  → Test
  → Git Commit (one logical milestone)
  → Repeat
```

## Rules

1. Update `docs/` (and an ADR when the choice is non-obvious) before writing new subsystem code.
2. Implement only what the notebook specifies—no silent scope expansion.
3. Test before committing.
4. Each commit is one logical milestone for that loop pass.
5. If tests reveal a design change, update the notebook before the next implementation pass.
